      Every word this app shows a person.

      One file, in Chinese, because this app has one audience and no plans for a
      second. The text is here rather than in the screens for the usual reason —
      one place to read, one place to change —and because a sentence split
      across Kotlin string concatenation cannot be proof-read or searched for.

      Placeholders are positional (%1$s, %2$d) rather than sequential, because a
      sentence reworded later may reorder them.
